---
import { links } from "../../config/site";

// From `make bench` (forma/bench), runs `fixed` and `fixed-db-indexed`.
const stats = [
  {
    value: "~1 ms",
    label: "Forma's own time per message",
    detail:
      "On top of the LLM, median. About 4 ms with MongoDB, including 7 round trips to the database.",
  },
  {
    value: "18–49 MB",
    label: "Memory",
    detail: "From one conversation to 64 at once, with MongoDB.",
  },
  {
    value: "~3 ms",
    label: "CPU per message",
    detail:
      "The whole tool loop, streamed: 64 conversations at once keep a tenth of one core busy.",
  },
  {
    value: "6,400/s",
    label: "Messages per second",
    detail:
      "With an LLM that answers instantly and no database: the runtime's ceiling. 930/s with MongoDB.",
  },
];
---

<section class="shell section border-t">
  <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">
    Light enough for the smallest machine
  </h2>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed">
    An LLM takes seconds to answer; Forma adds milliseconds. A personal agent
    runs comfortably on the smallest machine a cloud sells, and the same server
    handles many conversations at once.
  </p>

  <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {
      stats.map((stat) => (
        <div class="bg-card text-card-foreground flex flex-col rounded-xl border p-6">
          <dt class="text-muted-foreground order-2 mt-1 text-sm font-medium">
            {stat.label}
          </dt>
          <dd class="font-display order-1 text-3xl font-semibold tabular-nums">
            {stat.value}
          </dd>
          <dd class="text-muted-foreground order-3 mt-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            {stat.detail}
          </dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed">
    Measured with <code class="font-mono">make bench</code> on an 8-core Apple Silicon
    laptop. Each message is a full tool loop: an LLM call that asks for a tool, the
    tool, and an LLM call that answers. The LLM is a mock, so the numbers are Forma's
    alone; MongoDB ran on the same machine, indexed, holding 50,000 other messages.
    Exporting traces over OpenTelemetry raises memory to about 50–70 MB. A cloud's
    shared CPU answers fewer messages per second, but memory and CPU per message carry
    over.
    <a
      href={links.bench}
      class="text-accent-text underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
      >Run it yourself</a
    >.
  </p>
</section>
